<BRK/><RID>29 CFR 1910.1000</RID><RTL>Air Contaminants</RTL><BRK/><BRK/><RID>29 CFR 1926.59</RID><RTL>Hazard Communication</RTL><BRK/><BRK/></REF></SPT><SPT><TTL>DEFINITIONS</TTL><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<TXT>Definitions are provided throughout this Section, generally in the paragraph where used, and denoted by capital letters.  The following definitions 
are used throughout this Section:</TXT><BRK/>
<OLG><BRK/>
<OLI>CEILING - interior tank surfaces that extend from the horizontal plane at the designated maximum water line upward, including the upper 
portion of the tank shell (walls), columns, structural steel, the underside of the roof plates and other steel components in this area.</OLI><BRK/>
<BRK/>
<OLI>BOWL - interior tank surfaces that extend from the horizontal plane at the designated maximum water line downward, including the tank walls, 
columns, piping, pipe supports, bottom plates, and other steel components in this area.</OLI><BRK/></OLG>
<BRK/></SPT>
<SPT><TTL>SUBMITTALS</TTL><BRK/>
<NTE><BRK/>
<AST/><BRK/>
<NPR>NOTE:  Review Submittal Description (SD) definitions in Section <SRF>01 33 00</SRF> SUBMITTAL PROCEDURES and edit the following 
